      "The Mets began as more than a normal expansion team. They were New York’s answer to the Giants and Dodgers leaving for California, so the blue and orange carried pieces of both lost clubs. Casey Stengel managed a roster filled with aging names, castoffs, and players asked to do more than they could. The baseball was often poor, but the team’s reason for existing was powerful from the first day.",
