      "Bobby Valentine’s first full season produced a 17-win improvement and the first winning record since 1990. John Olerud arrived in a smart trade and immediately brought patience and defense to first base. Alfonzo grew into a complete infielder, while Todd Hundley remained a power threat and Rick Reed emerged from nowhere to stabilize the rotation.",
      "The Mets stayed in the Wild Card race deep into the summer, giving Shea meaningful games after years of embarrassment. The roster did not have one overwhelming superstar; it won through depth, defense, and a manager willing to use every matchup. The Subway Series also began in regular-season play, adding a new level of attention to games against the Yankees.",
      "An 88–74 finish was not enough for October, but it changed the question around the franchise. The Mets were no longer asking how to become respectable. They were asking what final piece could carry a good roster into the playoffs. That search would soon lead to Mike Piazza and change the entire direction of the club.",
