      "José Reyes supplied the reason to look forward. He debuted at 19, brought immediate speed, and showed the athletic ability of a future star. Cliff Floyd played through pain and became a respected clubhouse voice, while Steve Trachsel quietly gave the rotation dependable innings. David Wright was still climbing through the minors behind them.",
