      "David Wright debuted in July and immediately looked comfortable. His line-drive swing, strong arm, and calm manner gave fans a second homegrown player to place beside Reyes. Mike Piazza remained the lineup’s biggest name, and Tom Glavine made the All-Star team, but the season’s real importance shifted toward the two young infielders.",
