      "Omar Minaya and new manager Willie Randolph gave the Mets a more ambitious direction. Pedro Martínez arrived with star power and pitched brilliantly, Carlos Beltrán signed the largest contract in club history, and the organization clearly intended to challenge Atlanta instead of waiting through another slow rebuild.",
