      "The Mets took first place in April and never gave it back. Reyes created pressure from the first pitch, Wright drove in runs, Beltrán tied the club home-run record, and Carlos Delgado added the left-handed power the lineup had needed. The club won 97 games and ended Atlanta’s run of 14 straight division titles.",
      "The concern was the rotation. Pedro Martínez broke down, and Orlando Hernández was injured just before the postseason. The Mets swept Los Angeles anyway, then fought St. Louis through seven tense NLCS games. Endy Chávez’s leaping catch and double play in Game 7 felt like the moment that would send Shea to the World Series.",
