      "The Mets lost the final game at Shea and missed the postseason by one game, repeating the heartbreak in a different shape. The closing ceremony followed immediately, with franchise legends walking onto the field while the current team absorbed another collapse. Shea deserved a joyful goodbye. Instead, fans left with history behind them and an uncertain new ballpark ahead.",
