      "Citi Field opened with wide gaps, high walls, and expectations that a new home would refresh the franchise. The first season instead became an injury list. Reyes, Beltrán, Delgado, and many others missed major time, leaving Wright as the only everyday star trying to hold together a lineup that changed constantly.",
      "The ballpark itself became part of the discussion. Its first design leaned heavily on the old Brooklyn Dodgers and did not display enough Mets history, while the dimensions punished home-run hitters. On the field, Johan Santana pitched well before his own season ended early, and the club never recovered from losing nearly its entire core.",
