      "The season contained two of the greatest pitching stories in franchise history. On June 1, Johan Santana threw the first Mets no-hitter after 50 years of waiting. The 134-pitch effort, Beltrán’s disputed foul ball, and Mike Baxter’s catch against the wall turned the night into a mix of joy and danger.",
