      "The Mets finished 74–88 for the second straight year. Harvey’s Tommy John surgery meant he would miss 2014, delaying the dream of pairing him with the young pitchers approaching from the minors. The season is remembered less for its record than for the brief period when one starter made Citi Field believe it was watching the beginning of something huge.",
