      "The Mets spent the first half trying to win every game 2–1. deGrom, Harvey, Syndergaard, and Matz gave the rotation enormous talent, but the lineup was weakened by injuries and offered almost no support. Wilmer Flores crying on the field during a reported trade that never happened became the emotional low point—and then the season turned.",
