      "Pete Alonso arrived and immediately broke the idea that a rookie needed time to adjust. He hit 53 home runs, won the Home Run Derby, earned Rookie of the Year, and gave Citi Field a new center of attention. Jeff McNeil hit .318 and made the All-Star team, while deGrom won a second straight Cy Young Award.",
      "The team began slowly and entered the second half below .500, then produced a long winning surge that briefly made the Wild Card race feel real. The clubhouse found energy through Alonso’s personality and a group of young hitters. The bullpen, especially expensive newcomer Edwin Díaz, gave away too many games for the comeback to hold.",
